KaiT2en-NixOS divergence: the AppleT2 Speaker device without the PCM split.

Upstream's HiFi profiles split the speaker PCM with an identity channel
map. That buys nothing but a second, user-selectable sink: WirePlumber
builds a loopback whose capture end sits in the output list beside the
DSP sink and feeds the same hardware node in parallel with the filter
chain. It cannot be disabled (the DSP's target goes with it) or hidden
(createSplitPCMLoopback hardcodes Audio/Sink after the monitor rules).
So Speaker points straight at hw:${CardId},0, and the companion DSP
patch (t2-dsp-speaker-dsp-only.patch) gives the resulting node the name,
layout and class its graph expects. The hardware still runs the same
format, channel count and rate. (Originally landed in-tree as fe14b8f;
moved here in the 2026-11-15 sync so modules/ stays byte-identical to
upstream.)

Applied by nix/pkgs/t2bce_audio-alsa-ucm-conf on top of the upstream
source (-p1 relative to modules/apple-t2-alsa-ucm-conf), together with
the DSP patch.

Drop condition: remove (with the DSP patch) when upstream's AppleT2
profiles stop splitting the speaker PCM, or the DSP patch is dropped.
Re-check every sync.

